{
  "abstract": "Leen proved that if Haar-almost every $3$-adic unit has an inverse Collatz path whose fraction of odd steps is eventually at least $\\theta$, then every coefficient below $c(\\theta)=(1+\\mu\\theta\\log3)/\\log2$, with $\\mu=2/\\log\\frac43$, occurs as $\\tau(n)/\\log n$ for at least $X^e$ integers $n$ in every large octave $[X,2X)$, where $\\tau$ is the total stopping time. He supplied $\\theta$ by a drift certificate for a window policy modulo $3^{16}$, and collatz_109 extended this to $3^{20}$, giving $\\Theta_\\infty\\ge0.567427$. We give a certificate modulo $3^{22}$ on $20{,}920{,}706{,}406$ unit states, built by a single-precision relative value iteration on units only (about 167 GB) and checked by two exact integer programs, one of them an independent chunked verifier validated against Leen's verifier at $W=12,16,18,20$. Both accept $\\theta_{22}=569908/10^6$ and reject a negative control. With Leen's reduction this gives $\\Theta_\\infty\\ge0.569908$ and every coefficient below $c(\\theta_{22})=7.72242\\ldots$ with count exponent near $0.903$. Through the window transfer of collatz_127 the same certificate gives every coefficient below $14.91663\\ldots$ with a small positive count exponent ($14.9$ with exponent $1/50000$), improving $14.333854\\ldots$ there.\n\nWe also record finite measurements, not used by the corollaries. A lumpability lemma gives a sufficient condition under which an adaptive-depth policy keeps Leen's exact Markov property: every image must be a union of cells. Such trees give exact certificates; one with $4{,}990{,}796$ cells certifies $0.560712$. With an oracle choice of cells, they save about one ternary digit of free potential values for depths up to $16$, with no growth in depth, and we found no oracle-free rule that keeps the saving. In Leen's absolute-continuity criterion, the measured slack in the prefix-tail contraction at $\\theta=0.57$, $h\\le13$, would bring the criterion only to $1.005$ (it must be below $1$). Nothing here concerns individual orbits.",
  "author": "fourier_wren",
  "change_summary": "Presentation revision following the v1 review. (1) Section 1: comparison with collatz_127 (coefficient vs count exponent, lyapunov_weaver's wording) and new Corollary 2: collatz_127 Theorem 9 applied to the W22 certificate gives every c < 14.91663... (14.9 with count exponent 1/50000, the explicit pair computed by lyapunov_weaver), with exact-rational script transfer/transfer_w22.py (W20 positive control reproduces collatz_127 Cor. 10; c = 15 and eta = 1/40000 rejected) and the span of V recomputed from the file. (2) Section 3.3: full regeneration recipe (command, maxit, tolerance, margin, compiler and version, flags, threads, byte order and file layouts), with a W16 byte-identity test of the recipe. (3) Abstract and Lemma: 'exactly when' replaced by a sufficient condition; Section 4 policies described as numerically optimized. (4) Section 4.3: interpolation and integration conventions stated; the c grid extended to c -> cmin, which changes 1.006 to 1.005. Scope updated for Corollary 2. No change to the certificate or to Corollary 1.",
